\par\par \uc2 National Desk; SECTA\par \b \uc2 U.S. Asks Justices to Block Texas' New  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Law, Opening a New Legal Front\b0\par\par\uc2 By Katie Benner and Adam Liptak \par \uc2 864 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 October 2021\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 16\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The Texas law prohibits most abortions after about six weeks, before many women are even aware they are pregnant.\par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON -- The Biden administration will ask the Supreme Court to block a Texas law that bans most abortions after six weeks of pregnancy while a challenge to it moves forward, a spokesman for the Justice Department said on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Last month, in a separate case brought by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers, the Supreme Court allowed the law to go into effect in a bitterly divided decision. The new challenge -- from a different party and based on different legal theories -- will let the justices take a fresh look at the law, known as Senate Bill 8.\par \par \uc2 The vote in the earlier case was 5 to 4, with Chief Justice \uc2 John G. Roberts Jr\uc2 . joining the court's three liberal members in dissent.\par \par \uc2 ''The Justice Department intends to ask the Supreme Court to vacate the Fifth Circuit's stay of the preliminary injunction against Texas Senate Bill 8,'' the spokesman, Anthony Coley, said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 It is not clear when the department will file its emergency application in the Supreme Court. Based on their usual practices, the justices are likely to move fairly quickly once the application has been filed and could render a decision in a week or so.\par \par \uc2 The Texas law, one of the strictest in the country, bans abortions at around six weeks of pregnancy, a time when many women may not yet know they are pregnant. It makes no exceptions for pregnancies resulting from rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 Supreme Court precedents prohibit states from banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before fetal viability, the point at which fetuses can sustain life outside the womb, or about 22 to 24 weeks into a pregnancy. That makes the Texas law unconstitutional under the controlling precedents.\par \par \uc2 But it was written to make it difficult to challenge in court.\par \par \uc2 Usually, a lawsuit seeking to block a law because it is unconstitutional would name state officials as defendants. But the Texas law bars state officials from enforcing it and instead deputizes private individuals to sue anyone who performs the procedure or ''aids and abets'' it.\par \par \uc2 The patient may not be sued, but doctors, staff members at clinics, counselors, people who help pay for the procedure, and even an Uber driver taking a patient to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic are all potential defendants. Plaintiffs, who do not need to live in Texas, have any connection to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  or show any injury from it, are entitled to $10,000 and their legal fees recovered if they win. Prevailing defendants are not entitled to legal fees.\par \par \uc2 Attorney General \uc2 Merrick B. Garland\uc2  has called the enforcement mechanism an ''unprecedented'' effort to bar women from their constitutionally protected right to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Last week, Judge Robert L. Pitman of the Federal District Court in Austin temporarily blocked the law in the case brought by the Justice Department, writing that he would ''not sanction one more day of this offensive deprivation of such an important right.''\par \par \uc2 He criticized the law's efforts to avoid judicial scrutiny.\par \par \uc2 ''Fully aware that depriving its citizens of this right by direct state action would be flagrantly unconstitutional,'' Judge Pitman wrote, ''the state contrived an unprecedented and transparent statutory scheme to do just that.''\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, a divided three-judge panel of the U.S. Court of Appeals for the Fifth Circuit, in New Orleans, stayed Judge Pitman's ruling, reinstating the law. The Biden administration will ask the Supreme Court to lift the stay.\par \par \uc2 The law immediately stopped most abortions in Texas when it went into effect at the start of September. Demand at clinics in nearby states like Oklahoma has surged as women in Texas seeking abortions after six weeks of pregnancy have been forced to travel out of state.\par \par \uc2 In the earlier Supreme Court ruling, the majority opinion was unsigned and consisted of a single long paragraph. It said the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers who had challenged the law in an emergency application to the court had not made their case in the face of ''complex and novel'' procedural questions. The majority stressed that it was not ruling on the constitutionality of the Texas law and did not mean to limit ''procedurally proper challenges'' to it.\par \par \uc2 ''The court's order is stunning,'' Justice \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2  wrote in dissent. ''Presented with an application to enjoin a flagrantly unconstitutional law engineered to prohibit women from exercising their constitutional rights and evade judicial scrutiny, a majority of justices have opted to bury their heads in the sand.''\par \par \uc2 The ruling last month fueled the hopes of opponents of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights as the court takes up a separate case involving a Mississippi that bans most abortions after 15 weeks. That case is a direct challenge to Roe v. Wade, the landmark 1973 decision that established a constitutional right to the procedure.\par \par \uc2 The Justice Department is suing over the law's unique enforcement mechanism, which uses private individuals to enforce it. (PHOTOGRAPH BY KENNY HOLSTON FOR THE NEW YORK TIMES) \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020211016ehag0003s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
